{%- doc -%}
  The tinted panel a form is replaced by once it has been sent (Figma: 508:12684 on
  the corporate quote, 508:12824 on the wholesale application — the same panel with
  different words and one button instead of two).

  Chrome only: the light blue ground, the 20px corners, the star, and the rhythm the
  file sets inside — 48 from the star to the words, 16 between the headline and the
  copy, 48 again down to the buttons. What goes in it is the caller's, captured and
  passed as `content`, because those are blocks a merchant edits and this snippet
  should not know what they say.

  The 48 below the copy is the caller's to place on its own buttons: the column here
  runs at 16 so a headline and its paragraph sit together, and a row of buttons adds
  the other 32.

  @param {string} content - The captured markup that goes in the panel.
  @param {string} [class] - Additional CSS classes.

  @example
  {%- capture sent -%}{% content_for 'block', type: '_ui-heading', id: 'sent-heading' %}{%- endcapture -%}
  {% render 'ui-confirmation-panel', content: sent %}
{%- enddoc -%}

<div class="ui-confirmation-panel{% if class != blank %} {{ class }}{% endif %}">
  <span class="ui-confirmation-panel__star" aria-hidden="true">
    {{- 'icon-ui-sparkle.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
  </span>

  <div class="ui-confirmation-panel__content">
    {{ content }}
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .ui-confirmation-panel {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    inline-size: 100%;
    /* The file gives the panel no inline padding — the copy inside is capped
       instead. On a phone the panel is the page column and the caps never come
       into it, so it needs the padding the file did not have to write down. */
    padding: 32px 24px 48px;
    border-radius: 20px;
    background-color: var(--ui-color-light-blue);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .ui-confirmation-panel__star {
    display: block;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    inline-size: 32px;
    block-size: 32px;
    color: var(--ui-color-primary);
  }

  .ui-confirmation-panel__star > svg {
    display: block;
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: 100%;
  }

  /* The panel declares no gap, so this is the whole of the 48 between the star and
     the headline. */
  .ui-confirmation-panel__content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 16px;
    inline-size: 100%;
    margin-block-start: 48px;
  }

  .ui-confirmation-panel__content > :is(.ui-heading, h1, h2, h3) {
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Drawn at 445 inside the 630 panel, so it wraps where the file wraps it rather
     than running the panel's full width. */
  .ui-confirmation-panel__content > :is(.ui-text, p) {
    margin: 0;
    max-inline-size: 445px;
  }

  /* 48 between the copy and the buttons: the column's own 16 and 32 more here. */
  .ui-confirmation-panel__content > .ui-link-row {
    margin-block-start: 32px;
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .ui-confirmation-panel {
      padding-inline: 16px;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
